#: scenes/menues/help_menu.tscn
msgid "MAIN_RULES_TEXT"
msgstr "Objective:\n"
"The goal of the game is to deceive your opponents. Liar’s Dice can be played with two or more players.\n"
"\n"
"Setup:\n"
"Each player receives 5 dice. At the start of a round, all players roll their dice and secretly look at their values.\n"
"\n"
"Gameplay:\n"
"Players take turns (counterclockwise) making bids, stating the number of dice of a certain value in play. Each new bid must be higher than the previous one:\n"
"\n"
"You can increase the number of dice.\n"
"You can raise the face value.\n"
"You cannot decrease the number of dice.\n"
"Ones are wild and count as any value.\n"
"\n"
"Examples:\n"
"'Three threes' is higher than 'two threes.'\n"
"'Two fours' is higher than 'two threes.'\n"
"\n"
"Instead of raising the bid, you may challenge the previous player's bid by saying 'Check'\n"
"\n"
"Checking:\n"
"When a player calls 'Check' all players reveal their dice:\n"
"If the total number of matching dice is less than the declared bid, the player who made the bid loses the round.\n"
"If the number is equal to or greater than the bid, the player who called 'Check' loses instead.\n"
"The losing player discards one die. The next round starts with the player who lost a die.\n"
"The last player with dice remaining wins the game."

